WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:05.840
HBS is looking to produce a variety 
game show in countries around the world,

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.600
and their first location 
is here in Loveland City!

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.820
And...

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.040
they came to <i>us</i> to form 
a business partnership!

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:13.840
What?!

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.060
By "HBS," you mean <i>the</i> HBS?!

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.440
The one with the highest variety 
show viewership in the US?

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.410
That huge American TV company?!

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:26.500
It seems that exclusive interview with 
Key was very popular in America, too.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.300
They want to work with
 the producer, meaning you!

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.460
You're kidding.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.950
This is unbelievable!

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.410
"And the first, celebrated guest will be...

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.990
the CEO of LFG"?!

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.330
This is the set?

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.980
Amazing... That's a leading 
American TV station for you.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.030
Your company is accepting funding from LFG.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.790
Don't act surprised over this.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.800
We're getting ready to start recording.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.160
CEO, if you could come this way, please.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.620
Don't let them look down on you.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.410
I'm amazed you got him to agree.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.400
It's because I was able to use the name "HBS."

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.710
He's not the type to be swayed by that.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.400
We have confidence that in terms of 
planning and bargaining capacity,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.180
no other company can beat us.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:20.510
After seeing these results, 
all I can do is nod in agreement.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.260
<i>Heck yeah!</i>

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:26.230
<i>The truth is, it wasn't nearly so simple.</i>

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.390
<i>In order to get Victor to consent 
to appearing on the show,</i>

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:34.000
<i>I researched things like estimated profits 
and benefits, and assembled reports.</i>

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.990
<i>When I submitted them, they came right back.</i>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.400
Report on Projected Gains and Potential Market 
Movement as a Result of Appearing on HBS's Variety Show 

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.710
<i>It was just day after day 
of being called an idiot.</i>

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.220
<i>Then, just before the deadline 
I'd agreed on with HBS...</i>

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.160
I see. I'll appear on the show.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:49.070
Really? Thank y—

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.500
You won't change your mind later, will you?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:56.210
My word is more certain than any contract.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.970
I had always planned to accept this offer.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.010
Huh?

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:05.700
It's plain as day that appearing on 
this show would be a plus for LFG.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:10.340
We researched HBS, as well. There was 
something I wanted to look into.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:11.570
Then why...

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:14.230
I tested you to see how 
persistent you would be.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:18.190
This experience should prove 
useful in other situations.

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:21.870
<i>I'm going to make sure 
this show is a success!</i>

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.960
<i>Plus, if one of the games
 could embarrass Victor...</i>

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.450
Um... Are you all right?

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.500
Huh? Yes.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:33.580
I believe we confirmed this 
with you in advance,

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:35.900
but the show will be an escape game in which

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.430
the contestants must escape this
building using both brains and brawn.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.800
What is this?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.470
It's sort of a really oppressive feeling...

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:46.020
It's very scary.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.350
For this episode, we've got high-performance 
cameras set up throughout the set,

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.390
but there won't be a 
single staff member present.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.440
Not even one?

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.160
A picture is worth a thousand words.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.400
While the CEO is getting ready, 
want to give it a try?

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.340
Me? Really?

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:04.410
I thought if you understood the flow, 
you might feel more at ease.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:06.870
That's true...

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.430
<i>Whether the feeling I had in 
that moment was a premonition</i>

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.480
<i>or fear from the memories 
I'd lost, I don't know.</i>

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.650
<i>The only thing that's certain</i>

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:21.470
<i>is that there was no way to 
escape the truth behind it.</i>

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:34.310
"It takes all the running you can do, 
to keep in the same place."

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:34.310
~The Red Queen Hypothesis~

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.540
<i>In this world, there exist 
unique powers known as "Evol,"</i>

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:42.780
<i>which are possessed by a very few.</i>

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:47.200
<i>Among them, some chose to fight 
their fate, to fight the world.</i>

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.850
<i>This is the story of these young "Evolvers."</i>

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.950
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.660
"Connected Memories"

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.450
Please, head inside.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.500
Um... I don't think I...

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.710
It's all right. Now, go!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:22.950
Huh?

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.220
Has it started already?

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.100
Hey, wait a minute!

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.140
Please!

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.650
So they're saying I have
 to escape from here?

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.820
What... was that?

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.300
I can't!

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.550
<i>Let me out of here! Someone, please!</i>

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:05.510
<i>Victor!</i>

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:20.950
Victor...

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.360
Are you stupid? You're not some lost child.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.580
Why are you here?

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.710
I was nearly locked up, too.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.410
What do you mean? What about the filming?

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.260
This show will never be broadcast.

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.450
What?

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.380
I should never have accepted the offer.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:47.570
Wait! I don't understand!

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:51.800
We'll talk after we get out of here.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.790
What's going on?

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:03.690
<i>Again...</i>

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:10.260
They're real?

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:11.070
Don't worry.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:25.550
This way.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:57.780
This place is...

00:07:58.360 --> 00:07:59.240
What's wrong?

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.480
Again...

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:09.090
This room... This building... I know them.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.420
You...

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.010
An Evolver...

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:20.100
Can you keep going?

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.070
<i>It's all the same as last time.</i>

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:25.900
<i>Why?</i>

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.210
Look out!

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:44.920
Look out!

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:51.510
Victor!

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:24.630
I will never let you go again.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.410
<i>From this moment on, I will be your shield!</i>

00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:00.990
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.000
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.920
Stop crying already.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:22.640
I'll give you some good snacks.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.100
Snacks?

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:27.850
I'll bring them tomorrow.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:42.670
Victor...

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:48.220
You're awake.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.110
I'll get the doctor.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:01.820
Her progress is excellent.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.780
She can be discharged in a week.

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:07.240
I wanted to talk to you about that.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.040
They said it isn't all that bad.

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:19.360
But it seems they need to run some tests.

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:22.010
You should expect to spend 
at least two weeks here.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.340
That long?

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.260
You were asleep for a week. Accept it.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:32.520
Were you here the whole time?

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.450
Of course.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:36.270
It's my fault this happened.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:46.720
Back during that kidnapping case, 
we were together, weren't we?

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:48.290
You remember?

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:50.440
Just a little, about you.

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:53.840
But why would HBS...

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:57.790
I'm sorry.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:01.220
You've been asleep for quite a while. 
It's a natural reaction.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:02.800
Let's talk while we eat.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:03.950
I'd like some fried chick—

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:04.810
No.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:11.700
Did you make this for me? Specially?

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.350
Never mind that. Hurry up and eat.

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:22.820
Huh?

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:25.850
It's fine if you don't want it.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.930
N-No, I'll eat it! I'll eat it!

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:33.950
It's delicious!

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:39.170
<i>Victor gave me a simple timeline 
of the events leading up to now.</i>

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:43.820
<i>Seventeen years ago, he was 
rescued from the institution.</i>

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:48.260
<i>From that day, when we were separated,
up until today, he searched for me</i>

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.730
<i>and pursued the identity of the perpetrator.</i>

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:55.990
<i>He learned there was an organization called 
"Black Swan" behind the kidnappings,</i>

00:13:56.340 --> 00:14:01.150
<i>and that they were currently 
among HBS's largest investors.</i>

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.150
<i>Hoping to find more clues,</i>

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.150
<i>he accepted the request 
to appear on the show.</i>

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:12.040
You mean filming the show was 
a trap Black Swan set for you?

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:14.330
That's what bothers me.

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:19.460
If I was their target, there was no need 
to set up something so complicated.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:21.390
Me?

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:22.920
I thought about that.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:28.450
But if you were their target, it's strange 
that we're able to talk like this.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.250
Why did they do it, then?

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:34.220
What were they trying to accomplish 
by faithfully recreating

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.230
the events of seventeen years ago?

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:38.200
What changed because of that incident?

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:40.270
What happened there?

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:43.080
My memories came back.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:46.070
My power went out of control.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:47.920
Out of control?

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:52.730
While you were unconscious, 
I wasn't able to keep my power in check.

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:55.790
Even considering my highly emotional 
state, that has never happened.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.960
I've seen the same thing 
happen to someone before.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:09.130
It seemed like they didn't understand 
what was happening, either.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:11.290
What were the circumstances?

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:14.930
I was... about to be killed...

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:20.500
Don't think about anything. 
Just get some rest.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:22.160
Leave everything to me.

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:23.920
Wait!

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:25.840
Never mind. Just behave yourself.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:28.940
<b>~One Week Later~</b>

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:29.650
What?!

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:32.040
Our company went to HBS to protest?!

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.980
Of course we did!

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:36.810
They let our precious president get hurt!

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:40.330
Then the CEO of LFG came in to mediate...

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.580
Vict—The CEO did that?

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.290
Instead of dealing with our small company,

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:48.100
he said it would be more convenient 
in many ways to deal with LFG.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.810
And he said that it hasn't been safe lately,

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:53.530
so he installed security 
officers in our building.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:16:00.270
Will you bring my tablet for me later?

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.230
<b>~Another Week Later~</b>

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.660
<i>Hello? Kiro?</i>

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.800
Congrats, Potato Chip Princess! 
You're being discharged today, right?

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:11.140
<i>That's been put off another week.</i>

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:13.200
<i>Apparently, they still have tests to run.</i>

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.640
Oh...

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.740
Then you should take the chance 
to rest as much as you can!

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.160
You've been working hard 
this whole time, after all.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.610
I wish I could, but...

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:25.740
Right! I have to tell you, too, Kiro.

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:27.980
The pictures from that time we were trapped

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:30.260
were of the place I was held 
when I was kidnapped.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.260
How did you...

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:35.710
I remembered. Just bits and pieces, though.

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:38.770
Kiro! Rehearsal's starting!

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:40.460
Oh, for crying out loud...

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:41.680
Sorry. I have to go.

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:42.640
Okay.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:45.620
I'm safe for now, so don't worry.

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.650
Let's meet up in person and talk about it.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.120
All right.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:51.090
Don't do anything crazy, okay?

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.780
<b>~Another Week Later~</b>

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.620
You know, rage is not just 
psychologically damaging.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.130
It's harmful to one's physical health, as well.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:10.630
But this is the second time!

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.300
Look.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:14.880
They bloomed on my veranda today.

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:17.570
What a beautiful bellflower.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:20.000
They don't usually bloom 
this time of year, do they?

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:22.890
To think it would on the exact 
day I come to visit you.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.640
One small miracle found.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.340
I'm sorry.

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:29.290
You took the trouble to visit and everything...

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:33.010
And before, too, the way 
you looked after me...

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:36.910
I just want to find out what Black Swan's 
objective is as quickly as possible.

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:40.370
And you never waver 
in that feeling, do you?

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.990
If anything, it's stronger than it was before.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:55.920
You think locking her up like 
that is in her best interest?

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:58.300
Outsiders can keep their 
opinions to themselves.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:02.710
No matter how you try to run, 
the truth will reach out its own hand to you.

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:04.720
There is no way to stop it.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:06.330
Not even with your power.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.540
Are you unhappy with my methods?

00:18:16.060 --> 00:18:18.530
I'm scared. Very scared.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:20.500
Of leaving things to me?

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:22.040
No, not that!

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.310
I'm part of this...

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.000
But I don't know anything. That scares me.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.920
Let's go out for a little while.

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:34.330
It's beautiful.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:39.250
When I want to ease my worries, 
I look down at the city like this

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:42.530
and think over the things 
I've accomplished so far.

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:46.790
You can do anything you want, 
just the way you want, with no trouble.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:49.190
I didn't think you ever worried about anything.

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:52.680
I'm not talking about work or my daily life.

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:54.590
Right now, what I'm worried about...

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:57.480
is whether or not I'll be able to keep you safe.

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:02.760
Seventeen years ago, you saved me.

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:06.560
This time, I was supposed to 
protect you. And yet...

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:14.250
Besides the incident, 
I remembered one more thing.

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:19.630
The boy who saved me from
 an accident when I was little...

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.230
It was you, wasn't it?

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:33.510
It's true that I saved you.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:37.650
But you saved me first.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:39.150
You kept me safe.

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:43.000
To think you'd be cheering <i>me</i> up...

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:50.570
I understand the danger 
of what I'm trying to do.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:55.560
And I know that if you protected me, 
I'd never have to confront that danger.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:59.430
Even so, I don't want to hide behind you.

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:02.180
That's not who I am.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:05.520
That's right.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:07.350
You've always been that kind of person.

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:09.170
That's why I...

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:30.290
I know what's inside! It's pudding!

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:34.790
See?

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:36.010
How'd you know?

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:39.000
I saw it yesterday. 
You made it for me, right?

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:43.980
It's delicious!

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:46.590
It's the best pudding I've ever had!

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:53.090
It's delicious!

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:54.770
It really is the best I've had.

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:57.480
<i>I'm looking for someone.</i>

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.150
<i>There was a possibility
 that this may lead to a clue.</i>

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:02.330
<i>Seventeen years.</i>

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:05.400
<i>For seventeen years...</i>

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:12.370
<i>Victor has been thinking about 
me and worrying for me.</i>

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:44.640
It's been so long since I was home!

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:56.020
There's something I want to tell you
 concerning the Task Force. 
Let me know when's a good time.

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:53.580
The Task Force?

00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:56.010
I wonder if something 
happened involving Evolvers.

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:00.130
<i>What was that?</i>

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:24.380
<i>To think someone would be hurt 
without my knowing...</i>

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.140
<i>When the things I believed 
in began to crumble away...</i>

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:29.590
<i>I firmed my resolve to grow stronger.</i>

00:23:29.590 --> 00:23:30.720
<i>Episode eight,</i>

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:34.930
"Room 404"

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:32.770
<i>"Room 404."</i>
